<title>USA: Ampal-American chairman Recht resigns.</title>
<headline>Ampal-American chairman Recht resigns.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ampal-American Israel Corp said Wednesday Chairman Shlomo Recht would resign effective December 31, due to an Israeli banking law.</p>
<p>The law prohibits an employee of Bank Hapoalim, from serving as chairman of a non-banking company like Ampal, the company said. Recht is a Bank Hapoalim employee.</p>
<p>Ampal said Chief Executive and President Lawrence Lefkowitz would assume the duties pending election of a new chairman.</p>
